{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _calculate_row_sum(row: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a given row.\"\"\"\n    return sum(row)\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    It associates each row with its sum, sorts them, and reconstructs the matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a list of (row_sum, row) tuples\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = _calculate_row_sum(row)\n        rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    # Sort the list based on row_sum (the first element of the tuple)\n    rows_with_sums.sort()\n\n    # Extract the original rows in sorted order\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in rows_with_sums]\n    return sorted_matrix"}
