{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def max_difference(tuple_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements in a list of numerical tuples.\n    Returns the maximum absolute difference found, or 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    for t in tuple_list:\n        diff = abs(t[0] - t[1])\n        if diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = diff\n    return max_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def max_difference(tuple_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum absolute difference between numbers in a list of tuples.\n    It iterates through each tuple, computes the absolute difference, and returns the maximum found.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_diff = 0\n    for a, b in tuple_list:\n        current_diff = abs(a - b)\n        max_diff = max(max_diff, current_diff)\n    return max_diff"}
