{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "def recursive_list_sum(input_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively flattens a list and sums all its numerical elements.\n    Handles nested lists by calling itself on sub-lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for element in input_list:\n        try:\n            # Attempt to treat the element as an iterable (another list)\n            # This will raise a TypeError if the element is not iterable (e.g., an int)\n            total_sum += recursive_list_sum(element)\n        except TypeError:\n            # If it's not iterable, assume it's a numerical element (an integer)\n            total_sum += element\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "def recursive_list_sum(input_list: list) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"Recursively flattens a list and sums all numerical elements within it.\n    Non-numerical, non-list elements are ignored during summation.\"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        if isinstance(element, list):\n            current_sum += recursive_list_sum(element)\n        elif isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            current_sum += element\n    return current_sum"}
