{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(elements: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the Pancake Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(elements) # Create a mutable copy of the input list.\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the unsorted prefix arr[0...curr_size-1].\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, curr_size):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position.\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Bring the maximum element to the front.\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            # Move the maximum element to its correct sorted position.\n            _flip(arr, curr_size - 1)\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _find_max_index(arr: List[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements of the list arr.\"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[i]\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\ndef pancake_sort(arr: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list containing the sorted integers.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a copy of the input list to sort, as the public function should return a new list.\n    sorted_arr = list(arr)\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the largest element in the current unsorted sublist.\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(sorted_arr, current_size)\n\n        # If the largest element is not already at its correct position.\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the largest element to the beginning of the list.\n            _flip(sorted_arr, max_idx)\n            # Move the largest element from the beginning to its correct sorted position.\n            _flip(sorted_arr, current_size - 1)\n\n    return sorted_arr"}
