{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds an integer solution (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\"\"\"\n\n    def extended_gcd(a_val: int, b_val: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Computes gcd(a_val, b_val) and Bezout coefficients x_prime, y_prime such that a_val*x_prime + b_val*y_prime = gcd.\"\"\"\n        if a_val == 0:\n            return (b_val, 0, 1)\n\n        gcd, x1, y1 = extended_gcd(b_val % a_val, a_val)\n        x = y1 - (b_val // a_val) * x1\n        y = x1\n        return (gcd, x, y)\n\n    # Handle edge case: a = 0 and b = 0\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        if n == 0:\n            return (0, 0)\n        else:\n            return None\n\n    # Handle edge case: a = 0, b != 0\n    if a == 0:\n        if n % b == 0:\n            return (0, n // b)\n        else:\n            return None\n\n    # Handle edge case: a != 0, b = 0\n    if b == 0:\n        if n % a == 0:\n            return (n // a, 0)\n        else:\n            return None\n\n    # General case: a != 0 and b != 0\n    gcd_val, x_prime, y_prime = extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Check solvability condition\n    if n % gcd_val != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Scale the coefficients to find a particular solution\n    k = n // gcd_val\n    x = x_prime * k\n    y = y_prime * k\n\n    return (x, y)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/162", "solution": "def sum_series(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the series (n - 2*i) for i from 0 to n // 2.\n    This function directly implements the specified mathematical series summation.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n // 2 + 1):\n        term = n - (2 * i)\n        total_sum += term\n    return total_sum"}
