{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of an integer.\n    Handles negative numbers by considering their absolute value to count set bits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        number = abs(number)\n\n    count = 0\n    while number > 0:\n        # Brian Kernighan's algorithm: Clears the least significant set bit\n        number &= (number - 1)\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number: int | float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a number.\n    Floats are truncated to integers, and the absolute value is used for counting.\"\"\"\n\n    num_int = int(number)\n    n = abs(num_int)\n\n    count = 0\n    while n > 0:\n        n &= (n - 1)\n        count += 1\n\n    return count"}
