{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if x is a majority element in the sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of x using binary search (bisect_left logic).\n    low = 0\n    high = n\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n\n    first_occurrence_idx = low\n\n    # If x is not found at first_occurrence_idx, or if it's out of bounds, it's not present.\n    if first_occurrence_idx >= n or arr[first_occurrence_idx] != x:\n        return False\n\n    # Check the element at first_occurrence_idx + n/2.\n    # If it is also x, then x is a majority element.\n    target_check_idx = first_occurrence_idx + n // 2\n\n    if target_check_idx < n and arr[target_check_idx] == x:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "class BinarySearchUtil:\n    \"\"\"Utility class for binary search operations on sorted arrays.\n    Provides methods to find the first and last occurrence of an element.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_first(self, arr: list[int], x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of element x in the sorted array arr.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def find_last(self, arr: list[int], x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of element x in the sorted array arr.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\ndef is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element x is a majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    An element is a majority element if it occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    util = BinarySearchUtil()\n    first_occurrence_index = util.find_first(arr, x)\n\n    if first_occurrence_index == -1:\n        return False  # Element not found in the array\n\n    last_occurrence_index = util.find_last(arr, x)\n    count = last_occurrence_index - first_occurrence_index + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
