{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits of the input number to 1.\n    This is achieved using a bitwise OR operation with a mask where all even bits are 1.\"\"\"\n    # A mask with all even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ...) set to 1.\n    # This mask is sufficiently large to cover common integer sizes (up to 128 bits).\n    mask = 0x55555555555555555555555555555555\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set all even bits in 'number' to 1\n    # without affecting the odd-indexed bits.\n    modified_number = number | mask\n\n    return modified_number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(list_of_tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of canonicalized tuples in a list.\n    Each tuple (a, b) is canonicalized to (min(a, b), max(a, b)).\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrences = {}\n    for a, b in list_of_tuples:\n        canonical_tuple = (min(a, b), max(a, b))\n        occurrences[canonical_tuple] = occurrences.get(canonical_tuple, 0) + 1\n    return occurrences"}
