{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total number of sequences of length n.\n    Each element must be a positive integer, greater than or equal to twice the previous, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int, m: int, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Recursively counts valid sequences starting from a given state.\"\"\"\n        # Base case: A sequence of the desired length 'n' has been formed.\n        if current_length == n:\n            return 1\n\n        # Pruning: If 2 * last_element exceeds 'm', no valid next element can be chosen.\n        next_start_value = 2 * last_element\n        if next_start_value > m:\n            return 0\n\n        count_for_path = 0\n        # Iterate through all valid possible next elements.\n        for next_element in range(next_start_value, m + 1):\n            count_for_path += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element, m, n)\n\n        return count_for_path\n\n    total_count = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible values for the first element of the sequence.\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_count += _count_sequences_recursive(1, first_element, m, n)\n\n    return total_count"}
