{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "class DigitFrequency:\n    \"\"\"Represents a digit and its frequency, with a method to check validity.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, digit_value: int, count: int):\n        self.digit_value = digit_value\n        self.count = count\n\n    def is_frequency_valid(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the digit's frequency is less than or equal to its value.\"\"\"\n        return self.count <= self.digit_value\ndef _calculate_digit_frequencies(number: int) -> dict[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the frequency of each digit in a given integer.\"\"\"\n    digit_counts = {}\n    num_str = str(abs(number))\n    for char_digit in num_str:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        digit_counts[digit] = digit_counts.get(digit, 0) + 1\n    return digit_counts\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates digit frequency validation based on the specified rule.\"\"\"\n    digit_counts = _calculate_digit_frequencies(number)\n\n    overall_valid = True\n    for digit, count in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_freq_obj = DigitFrequency(digit_value=digit, count=count)\n        if not digit_freq_obj.is_frequency_valid():\n            overall_valid = False\n            break\n    return overall_valid"}
