{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "def dict_depth(data: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum depth of nested dictionaries within the input data.\n    The depth is 1 for an empty dictionary or one with no nested dictionaries.\"\"\"\n    max_nested_depth = 0\n    for value in data.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            # Recursively find the depth of the nested dictionary.\n            nested_depth = dict_depth(value)\n            max_nested_depth = max(max_nested_depth, nested_depth)\n\n    # The current level adds 1 to the maximum depth found in its nested dictionaries.\n    return 1 + max_nested_depth"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    It follows L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(k)=L(k-1)+L(k-2) for k > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b"}
