{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of any contiguous subarray within a given list of integers.\n    The algorithm tracks the maximum and minimum product ending at the current position.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Assuming the input 'arr' is non-empty, based on typical problem constraints.\n    # Initialize max_prod, curr_max, and curr_min with the first element of the array.\n    max_prod = arr[0]\n    curr_max = arr[0]\n    curr_min = arr[0]\n\n    # Iterate through the array starting from the second element.\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = arr[i]\n\n        # Store the current maximum product before it's updated. This value is needed\n        # for calculating the new current_min, as curr_max will be redefined.\n        temp_curr_max = curr_max\n\n        # The new current_max can be the number itself, or num multiplied by the\n        # previous current_max, or num multiplied by the previous current_min (e.g., two negatives make a positive).\n        curr_max = max(num, num * temp_curr_max, num * curr_min)\n\n        # Similarly, the new current_min can be the number itself, or num multiplied by the\n        # previous current_max, or num multiplied by the previous current_min.\n        curr_min = min(num, num * temp_curr_max, num * curr_min)\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        max_prod = max(max_prod, curr_max)\n\n    return max_prod"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of any contiguous subarray within a given array of integers.\n    Handles positive, negative, zero, and empty arrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_product = arr[0]\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        num = arr[i]\n\n        # Store previous max_so_far because min_so_far update needs it\n        temp_max_so_far = max_so_far\n\n        max_so_far = max(num, temp_max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n        min_so_far = min(num, temp_max_so_far * num, min_so_far * num)\n\n        max_product = max(max_product, max_so_far)\n\n    return max_product"}
