{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given non-negative integer.\n\n    Args:\n        number: A non-negative integer (number >= 0).\n\n    Returns:\n        The last digit of the factorial of 'number' (an integer between 0 and 9).\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input 'number' is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    elif number >= 5:\n        return 0  # BR3: For N >= 5, last digit of N! is 0\n    elif number == 0:\n        return 1  # BR4: 0! = 1\n    elif number == 1:\n        return 1  # BR5: 1! = 1\n    elif number == 2:\n        return 2  # BR6: 2! = 2\n    elif number == 3:\n        return 6  # BR7: 3! = 6\n    elif number == 4:\n        return 4  # BR8: 4! = 24\n    return -1 # Should not happen, indicates an unhandled case"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/578", "solution": "def interleave_lists(list1: list, list2: list, list3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Interleaves three lists of the same length into a single flat list.\n    Appends elements from list1, list2, then list3 sequentially for each index.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(list1)\n    result = []\n    for i in range(length):\n        result.append(list1[i])\n        result.append(list2[i])\n        result.append(list3[i])\n    return result"}
