{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "def perfect_squares(num1: int, num2: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a sorted list of perfect squares within a specified integer range.\n    The list is ordered in ascending order, or is empty if no perfect squares are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n\n    # Determine the smallest integer 'i' such that i*i >= num1.\n    if num1 <= 0:\n        start_root = 0\n    else:\n        s_candidate = int(num1**0.5)\n        if s_candidate * s_candidate < num1:\n            start_root = s_candidate + 1\n        else:\n            start_root = s_candidate\n\n    # Determine the largest integer 'j' such that j*j <= num2.\n    if num2 < 0:\n        end_root = -1  # Ensures the loop range is empty if num2 is negative.\n    else:\n        end_root = int(num2**0.5)\n\n    # Iterate from start_root to end_root (inclusive) and collect the squares.\n    for i in range(start_root, end_root + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        # The defined start_root and end_root calculations ensure\n        # that 'square' is already within the [num1, num2] range.\n        result.append(square)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(a: int, b: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies all perfect squares within the inclusive integer range [a, b].\n    Returns an empty list if a > b or no perfect squares are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a > b:\n        return []\n\n    results = []\n\n    # Calculate the starting and ending integer square roots for the iteration.\n    start_sqrt = math.ceil(math.sqrt(max(0, a)))\n    end_sqrt = math.floor(math.sqrt(b))\n\n    for i in range(int(start_sqrt), int(end_sqrt) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        # Add the square to results if it falls within the given range.\n        if a <= square <= b:\n            results.append(square)\n\n    return results"}
