{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(arr1, arr2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th smallest element from two given sorted arrays.\n    It uses a two-pointer approach to efficiently locate the element.\n    \"\"\"\n    p1, p2 = 0, 0\n    kth_element = 0\n\n    while p1 < len(arr1) and p2 < len(arr2):\n        if arr1[p1] < arr2[p2]:\n            kth_element = arr1[p1]\n            p1 += 1\n        else:\n            kth_element = arr2[p2]\n            p2 += 1\n        k -= 1\n        if k == 0:\n            return kth_element\n\n    while p1 < len(arr1):\n        kth_element = arr1[p1]\n        p1 += 1\n        k -= 1\n        if k == 0:\n            return kth_element\n\n    while p2 < len(arr2):\n        kth_element = arr2[p2]\n        p2 += 1\n        k -= 1\n        if k == 0:\n            return kth_element"}
