{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\n    It builds a table of Stirling numbers of the second kind to compute the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D list `stirling` to store Stirling numbers of the second kind, S(i, j).\n    # `stirling[i][j]` will store S(i, j).\n    stirling = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers: S(0, 0) = 1.\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table using the recurrence relation: S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j).\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\\\n        # Base case: S(i, 0) = 0 for i > 0.\\\n        stirling[i][0] = 0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling[i][j] = stirling[i-1][j-1] + j * stirling[i-1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number B_n is the sum of Stirling numbers of the second kind S(n, k) for k from 0 to n.\n    nth_bell = sum(stirling[n][k] for k in range(n + 1))\n\n    return nth_bell"}
