{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "import math\ndef max_of_nth(matrix, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the n-th column of a given matrix.\n    Raises ValueError or IndexError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Column index n must be non-negative.\")\n\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix cannot be empty.\")\n\n    max_value = float('-inf')\n\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) <= n:\n            raise IndexError(\"Row is too short for column n.\")\n\n        element = row[n]\n        if element > max_value:\n            max_value = element\n\n    return max_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "def merge(input_list: list[list[any]]) -> list[list[any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a list of two-element sublists into a list of two sublists.\n    The first collects all first elements, the second collects all second elements, preserving order.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_elements_list = []\n    second_elements_list = []\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        first_elements_list.append(sublist[0])\n        second_elements_list.append(sublist[1])\n\n    return [first_elements_list, second_elements_list]"}
