{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates, including the given coordinate itself.\n    Adjacency is defined as all coordinates within a 3x3 grid centered on the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    x_center, y_center = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):\n        current_x = x_center + dx\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):\n            current_y = y_center + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([current_x, current_y])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all 9 adjacent coordinates, including the central one, for a given 2D coordinate.\n    Coordinates are returned in a specific order: x-offset then y-offset from -1 to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for x_offset in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for y_offset in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            new_x = x + x_offset\n            new_y = y + y_offset\n            adjacent_coords.append([new_x, new_y])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
