{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the bitwise XOR of all unique pairs in a list of numbers.\n    It iterates through all pairs (numbers[i], numbers[j]) where i < j and sums their XORs.\"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            total_xor_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n    return total_xor_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Creates a new list to store the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = input_list[:]  # Create a mutable copy of input_list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Build a max-heap.\n    # The last parent node is at index n//2 - 1.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Swap root (largest) with current last element\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the input list in-place using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It modifies the input list directly and returns the sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    _build_max_heap(input_list)\n\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        input_list[i], input_list[0] = input_list[0], input_list[i]\n        _heapify(input_list, i, 0)\n\n    return input_list"}
