{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "import math\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r: float, h: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a right circular cone given its radius and height.\n    It first computes the slant height and then applies the lateral surface area formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the slant height 'l' using the Pythagorean theorem\n    l = math.sqrt(r**2 + h**2)\n\n    # Calculate the lateral surface area using the formula pi * r * l\n    lateral_surface_area = math.pi * r * l\n\n    return lateral_surface_area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "class ListLengthMismatchError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when input lists for summation have different lengths.\n    It indicates that the element-wise operation cannot proceed due to a mismatch.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\ndef sum_list(list_a: list[int | float], list_b: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the element-wise sum of two input lists, ensuring they are of equal length.\n    Raises ListLengthMismatchError if input list lengths do not match.\"\"\"\n    if len(list_a) != len(list_b):\n        raise ListLengthMismatchError(\"Input lists must be of equal length.\")\n\n    result_list = []\n    for i in range(len(list_a)):\n        result_list.append(list_a[i] + list_b[i])\n    return result_list"}
