{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list by k positions to the right.\n    Returns a new list with elements rotated.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    # Calculate the effective number of rotations\n    k_eff = k % n\n\n    # Split the list into two parts and concatenate them:\n    # the last k_eff elements followed by the first (n - k_eff) elements.\n    rotated_list = input_list[n - k_eff:] + input_list[:n - k_eff]\n    return rotated_list"}
