{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "def toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Toggles all bits of an integer except its most significant bit (MSB) and least significant bit (LSB).\n    The LSB is considered the bit at position 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the position of the most significant bit (MSB).\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # The least significant bit (LSB) is at position 0.\n    lsb_pos = 0\n\n    # Calculate the number of bits strictly between MSB and LSB.\n    num_middle_bits = msb_pos - (lsb_pos + 1)\n\n    # Create a bitmask for the middle bits.\n    if num_middle_bits <= 0:\n        mask = 0\n    else:\n        # Construct a sequence of 'num_middle_bits' ones and shift it to the correct position.\n        mask = ((1 << num_middle_bits) - 1) << (lsb_pos + 1)\n\n    # Toggle the middle bits by XORing the number with the generated mask.\n    return number ^ mask"}
