{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "def check_min_heap(array: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a valid min-heap.\n    Handles empty and single-element arrays as valid min-heaps.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only up to the last potential parent node.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_idx < n and array[i] > array[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_idx < n and array[i] > array[right_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "def check_min_heap(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a valid min-heap.\n    Iterates through non-leaf nodes, ensuring parent values are less than or equal to their children.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # An empty array or an array with one element is a valid min-heap.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only through non-leaf nodes.\n    # In a 0-indexed array, non-leaf nodes are from index 0 to (n // 2) - 1.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_idx < n:\n            if arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n                return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_idx < n:\n            if arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n                return False\n\n    # If no violations were found, the array is a min-heap.\n    return True"}
